Z||000006||Richard Parnell||02-25-2000||01:50 PM||||I used to paint t-shirts also years ago at hot rod shows up in Tacoma Washington.  When I was a kid of course.  I was inspired by Big Daddy.  I was just thinking, even tho it's been a while I should try and draw up some hot rod style cartoons for t-shirts of Fieros.  Flames coming out the exhaust. Dark interior with eerie looking eyes staring out.  Shifter sticking out the t-top.  Front wheels off the ground. Ohhyeahh, I think I'm inspired.||||reg||6
Z||000007||SpeedPhreak||02-25-2000||02:22 PM||||Rat Fink & Roth are still big in airbrushing circles.  especially the custom auto painters.  i have recent airbrush action magazines that are dedicated to him, his art, &/or the style he inspired.  he is too cool.||||reg||1
Z||000008||lowCG||02-27-2000||09:25 PM||||I just saw 'ol Ed today,at the Detroit Autorama,he's got shift knobs now that are a characture(sp?) of himself,and is showing a neat little mid engined car with a Goe,Metro engine in back.Totally cool dude.<BR>I really just needed to go and do my laundry today,but,since the Auto show was in the same direction as the laundromat...||||reg||1
Z||000009||kidzwheelz||02-28-2000||10:25 PM||||  I met "Big Daddy" at the Salt Lake City Autorama two years ago. What a guy! He is still into the rodding scene real heavy. The guy just cracks me up. There's definitely something to be said for a guy with that much personality. Wish he'd share the wealth with a couple of other people I have met. (Boyd Coddington comes to mind here!!!)||||reg||1
